Join orders with customers on customer_id to add customer_name to each order in Capybara DSL:

```capybara
PIPELINE task {
    SOURCE orders: TABLE[id: INT?, customer_id: INT?, amount: DECIMAL?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/orders.parquet");
    SOURCE customers: TABLE[id: INT?, name: STRING?, email: STRING?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/customers.parquet");
    STEP joined = JOIN { TYPE LEFT; ON left.customer_id == right.id; }
    STEP selected = SELECT { COLUMNS id, customer_id, amount, name AS customer_name; }
    SINK result = PARQUET(file: "output.parquet");
    FLOW { orders -> joined.left; customers -> joined.right; joined -> selected -> result; }
}
```

