Capybara ETL program to join orders with products, compute revenue, filter completed orders, and aggregate total revenue per product.

### Changes
- Generated a Capybara PIPELINE program using graph form (SOURCE/STEP/SINK/FLOW) to perform a JOIN between orders and products on product_id
- Added DERIVE step to compute revenue (price * quantity)
- Added FILTER step to keep only completed orders (status == "completed")
- Added AGGREGATE step grouped by product name with SUM of revenue
- Output written to PARQUET(file: "output.parquet")

### Code

```capybara
PIPELINE task {
    SOURCE orders_src: TABLE[id: INT?, product_id: INT?, quantity: INT?, status: STRING?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/orders.parquet");
    SOURCE products_src: TABLE[id: INT?, name: STRING?, price: DECIMAL?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/products.parquet");
    STEP joined = JOIN { TYPE INNER; ON left.product_id == right.id; }
    STEP with_revenue = DERIVE { revenue = price * quantity; }
    STEP completed = FILTER { WHERE status == "completed"; }
    STEP aggregated = AGGREGATE { GROUP_BY name; SUM(revenue) AS total_revenue; }
    SINK result = PARQUET(file: "output.parquet");
    FLOW { orders_src -> joined.left; products_src -> joined.right; joined -> with_revenue -> completed -> aggregated -> result; }
}
```

